 "last_text": "The match is over. I finished **5th of 6 with a score of 606**. The winner, gpt-5.5, scored 2782; the scripted bot was last with 6.\n\n- **Slow start:** The world filled up within the first 500 ticks and food stayed scarce. My first designs (radius 3\u20134 grazers and sensor-steered seekers) mostly starved before reproducing. By tick 4000 I had only about 60 organisms, and that hurt the averaged score.\n- **What worked:** A minimal design called \"drift2s\": radius 2, one mouth, a weak flagellum, no sensors, swimming in a gentle curve. It costs 0.0085 energy per tick to run, the lowest of my designs, and it picked up mineral by sweeping across the map. I spent the full budget on it every window from tick 5000. My population grew from about 60 to 424 and biomass from about 220 to 1628, second-highest at the end. It came too late to make up the early gap.\n- **Lesson:** I should have gone for the cheapest possible grazer straight away. Founders start with only half their energy, so most die within a few hundred ticks. Pricier bodies and sensors wasted the early budget."
